             ,HELPFUL HINTS

,FOR EVERYONE3 ,MAKE THE SHAPES WITH
  YOUR HANDS3 FOR BROAD1 SPREAD BOTH
  HANDS WIDE2 FOR OVAL1 MAKE AN EGG WITH
  YOUR HANDS2 FOR SMALL1 BRING TWO
  FINGERS CLOSE TOGETHER2 FOR LONG AND
  NARROW1 MOVE YOUR HANDS FAR APART4
,VISION3 ,TOUCH REAL LEAVES TO FIND OUT
  THEIR SHAPE4 ,RUN A FINGER ROUND THE
  EDGE OF THE LEAF3 IS IT BROAD1
  EGG-LIKE1 SMALL1 OR LONG AND THIN8
,MOVEMENT3 ,IF WRITING IN THE TABLE IS
  HARD1 HAVE A PHOTO OF THE PLANTS TAKEN
  EVERY THIRD DAY1 OR SAY YOUR
  OBSERVATION ALOUD AND LET A PARTNER
  WRITE IT4
,FOR TEACHERS3 ,DO THE PROJECT IN PAIRS3
  ONE CHILD WATERS THE PLANT1 AND THE
  OTHER LOOKS AND SAYS WHAT THEY SEE4
  ,INSTEAD OF WRITING IN THE TABLE1 LET
  CHILDREN DRAW A SMILING FACE IF THE
  PLANT IS FINE OR A SAD FACE IF THE
  PLANT HAS WILTED4 ,AFTER THE
  EXPERIMENT PUT THE INDOOR PLANT IN THE
  SUN TOO SO THAT IT RECOVERS4

